test_new_image_with_location: Do not rely on DNS resolution

Backport of upstream commit a37c43135e (master, 2026-09-28, Change-Id
I8ec68ff70e18fab68ed6a90fe30a1bbfc28c715c), cherry-picked to
stable/2026.2 as a3e5f490b7 (2026-09-30). No glance tag contains it:
33.0.0 is the newest 33.x tag as of 2026-10-10, and it resolves to the
same commit as 33.0.0.0rc1.

`TestImageFactory.test_new_image_with_location`
(glance/tests/unit/test_store_image.py) builds an image whose location
is `http://storeurl.com/container/<uuid>` (BASE_URI). Glance 33.0.0
added an SSRF filter for HTTP(S) locations: `_check_location_uri`
(glance/location.py) calls `store_utils.validate_external_location`,
which for `http` and `https` returns `validate_uri`
(glance/common/utils.py), and `get_validated_address` resolves the host
with `socket.getaddrinfo`. The domain storeurl.com answers NXDOMAIN
since about 2026-10-09, so the lookup raises `socket.gaierror`, the
location is rejected before any store backend runs, and the test fails
with `BadStoreUri: Invalid location`. The test-service-images job of
the Build Images workflow has been red on every run since, on main and
on every pull request, with this one failure out of 2423 tests. A suite
that has to resolve a public host cannot pass without DNS either.

The upstream change mocks `glance.common.utils.socket.getaddrinfo` for
that one test and returns a single fake address, so the validation
never touches the resolver. The hunk is carried verbatim, comment text
and fake address included, so that the patch reverse-applies on the
first tag that contains the upstream commit and can be retired then.

The patch changes a test module only and nothing in the built image,
so tests/container-images/verify_glance.sh carries no assertion for
it.

No 2026.1 twin: glance 32.0.0 has no validate_uri, so the test never
resolves the host and the 2026.1 leg stays green.

Applies to glance 33.0.0 (2026.2).

Upstream status: merged on master as a37c43135e, backported to
stable/2026.2 as a3e5f490b7 (2026-09-30).

diff --git a/glance/tests/unit/test_store_image.py b/glance/tests/unit/test_store_image.py
index a00832f..185ee69 100644
--- a/glance/tests/unit/test_store_image.py
+++ b/glance/tests/unit/test_store_image.py
@@ -1323,7 +1323,13 @@ class TestImageFactory(unit_test_base.StoreClearingUnitTest):
         self.assertEqual('private', image.visibility)
         self.assertEqual([], image.locations)
 
-    def test_new_image_with_location(self):
+    @mock.patch("glance.common.utils.socket.getaddrinfo")
+    def test_new_image_with_location(self, mock_getaddrinfo):
+        # This avoid internet access in validate_external_location()
+        # (ie: DNS resolution of storeurl.com)
+        mock_getaddrinfo.return_value = [
+            (None, None, None, None, ('93.184.216.34', 80))
+        ]
         locations = [{'url': '%s/%s' % (BASE_URI, UUID1),
                       'metadata': {}}]
         image = self.image_factory.new_image(locations=locations)
